



Implement the smallest safe SUITE context cleanup.

The existing lifecycle integration already releases
INVOCATION, CLASS and TEST contexts when their
owning TestNG test context finishes.

Requirements:

1. Reuse the existing lifecycle listener,
   coordinator and context registry.

2. Handle ISuiteListener.onFinish(ISuite).

3. Resolve the SUITE context owned by the
   finishing TestNG suite.

4. Verify all child TEST contexts have already
   been released.

5. Release the SUITE context through the
   existing lifecycle coordinator.

6. Remove its ownership mapping and
   configuration layers.

7. Never release a SUITE context with live
   children or active bindings.

8. Preserve fail-fast behavior for invalid
   lifecycle transitions.

9. Keep ROOT registered. ROOT cleanup will
   be handled separately.

10. Do not introduce new global state or
    another listener coordinator.

11. Do not modify legacy listeners.

Add real TestNG 7.12.0 integration tests verifying:

- One suite containing two parallel test elements.
- Both test elements share the same SUITE context.
- CLASS, TEST and INVOCATION cleanup occurs first.
- The SUITE context remains available until
  suite completion.
- The SUITE context is released at onFinish(ISuite).
- ROOT remains registered.
- No orphan layers or ownership mappings remain.
- Two independent suites cannot release each
  other's contexts.

Run the relevant integration tests and the
complete module test suite.

Report failures without weakening assertions.
